[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1196","stub":{"id":"1196","section":"Stillwater (Main St.) to Delaware River","altname":"","river":"Paulins Kill","difficulty":"ItoII","states":["USA-NJR"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"105","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"108159","location":{"latitude":"41.0099983215332","longitude":"-74.5199966430664"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"113401","location":{"latitude":"41.0331001281738","longitude":"-74.8741149902344"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"17","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101246588","title":null,"post_date":"2010-03-16 04:00:00+00","detail":"i paddled 2 sections of the paulinskill in the past 3 days. not much to report on the section above paulinskill lake except the the dam has a bad hydrolic @ high levels i'd guess 2000cfs and up maybe even less(i ran @ 2770) and the boogie directly after changes dramatically @ the higher flow. the section below paulinskill lake has 2 hazards. the first is a log jam that completely blocks the river under the old orchard rd bridge,see pic, i portaged on river left. a bit further down river are 3 small rapids spaced about 30 yards apart there is a HUGE tree stuck in the first feature blocking almost the whole river, sneak around the left side or portage river right on E. crisman rd. thats all for now, see ya on the river.","user":{"name":"dave carter"}}],"photos":[{"id":"872752","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872753","description":"","caption":"old orchard rd bridge","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872752","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872752"}}],"detail":{"id":"1196","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"The Putin is a little bridge about 50 yards from Stillwater General Store... The first 4 miles are mostly flatwater except for Stonebridge Damn... the Damn is small and there is a break towards the right side where you can go over it... the next damn is at Crisman Road... this one is not kayak friendly... the water crashes directly onto concrete... you can easily get out on the right side and walk to the bottom of the damn... or take out there to make it a quick 2 hour paddle.\n\n...more to come...\n\nGPS coordinates will be updated soon... current coords are approximate...","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"17","correlations":[{"reachID":"1196","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"250","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"3000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"Paulins Kill at Blairstown NJ","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01443500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"105","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.83","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"40.9808333","longitude":"-74.9533333"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/01443500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/01443500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"105","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs",